ce category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9172901-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9172901</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ELECTRON PROPERTY RESEARCH INS</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IDO KATSUTOMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ELECTRON PROPERTY RESEARCH INSTITUTE CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IDO, KATSUTOMI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IDO KATSUTOMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IDO, KATSUTOMI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An apparatus (32) for feeding fish and shellfish wherein pearl oysters (11) can be stably fed. Pearl oysters and water for feeding are contained in a feeding water tank (12). The water in the feeding water tank is supplied into a decomposition tank (19) wherein discharges of the pearl oysters formed in the feeding water tank are decomposed to give processed water thus purified. In a feed-culture tank (23), a feed liquor for the pearl oysters is cultured. The processed water is supplied into the feed-culture tank. Fluorescent lamps (24) flash over the feed-culture tank.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un dispositif d'alimentation (32) pour poissons et crustacés dans lequel des huîtres perlières (11) peuvent être alimentées de façon stable. Les huîtres perlières et l'eau destinée à l'alimentation se trouvent dans un réservoir d'eau d'alimentation (12). L'eau du réservoir d'alimentation passe dans un réservoir de décomposition dans lequel les déjections libérées dans l'eau d'alimentation par les huîtres perlières, sont décomposées, et où l'eau est traitée et purifiée. Dans un réservoir de culture, on cultive une liqueur nutritive pour les huîtres perlières. Des lampes fluorescentes (24) clignotent au-dessus du réservoir de culture.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>